{"id": "bd2ef86a-bbe6-488d-b7ad-f12b7cde3c2b", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Looking at the config, the S3 ARN wildcard covers all buckets so logs-a, data-b, and data-c object events are captured for both reads and writes. But there's no Lambda function data resource specified, meaning fn-x and fn-y invocations aren't logged at the data event level.

I should note caveats — this only covers buckets owned by the trail's account, Lambda invoke calls are data events (unlike CreateFunction, which is management), and I'm basing this entirely on the pasted config since I can't query CloudTrail directly through available tools.

